{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter and Online Dating", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How Do I Do This?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking for Help or Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are several ways to ask for help in English. You can use polite and casual language to do this.  Let's look at one particular structure for asking for help.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the structure:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Can</span>/<span class=\"strong\">Could</span>/<span class=\"strong\">Do</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">you</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">verb</span> +  <span class=\"strong\">me (optional)</span> + <span class=\"strong\"> question word</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me what you would do if you were me?</span><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Could you show me how to choose the perfect spot?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Do you have any idea where to find this perfect setting?</span><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Can/Could/Do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" (me)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Question Word\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" you \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">what</span> I should wear for a blind date?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" you \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" show\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">how </span>to arrange the perfect date?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" you \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">any</span> idea where to find the perfect setting?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">where</span> I can find a place that is quiet, but not too quiet?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Can</span> is the more casual choice of wording to ask for help or advice. <span class=\"strong\">Could</span> is more formal. <span class=\"strong\">Do you have ... ?</span> is also quite formal in usage. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use subject and object relative clauses when you want to make it clear which person or thing you are talking about.<br/><br/>Relative clauses begin with relative pronouns. <br> <br> You use the pronoun<span class=\"italic\"> who</span> to refer to people, <span class=\"italic\">which</span>  to refer to things or <span class=\"italic\">that</span> to refer to either people or things. You put the relative clause immediately <span class=\"underline\">after the noun</span> it talks about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"underline\">subject relative clause</span> describes the subject of the clause.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The school that I went to is over there.</span><br/> Which school? The school I went to.<br/> The clause <span class=\"italic\">that I went to</span> immediately follows school - the noun it describes", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An <span class=\"underline\">object relative clause</span> describes the object of the clause.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Can you remember the name of the movie that we saw?</span><br/> Which movie? The movie we saw.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Relative Pronoun \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Type of Relative Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">A first date should feel like a relaxing experience, which is the most important part.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" which is the important part\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">which</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The people who sit around you shouldn't have to shout.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" who sit around you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">who</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You must choose a place that you're familiar with.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" that you're familiar with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">object</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "worried", "type": "name"}, {"content": "troubled about potential problems; anxious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You look worried. What's the matter?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about a first date.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "relaxing", "type": "name"}, {"content": " causing someone to feel less tense or anxious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A first date should feel like a relaxing experience", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "setting", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way a place is set up and decorated", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think the restaurant setting is important for a first date.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dim", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not brightly lit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The lighting should be dim and not too bright.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chatter", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the noise made by several conversations at once", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't want to be distracted by people's chatter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to drown out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be so loud that something cannot be heard", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should avoid loud bars that drown out your conversation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "comfort zone", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a situation in which you feel the most at ease", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You shouldn't get out of your comfort zone on the first date.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of 3 question people often  ask about relationships. Write them on 3 pieces of paper. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give your questions to a partner. Take your partner's questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer your partner's questions in the style of a relationship advice column.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can go online to read about relationship advice columns for help.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange your answers with your partner. React to your partner's answers.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss complex subjects.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about relationships and friendships.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express opinions and reactions.", "type": "text"}]}], "l